"en":"Cloud Pattern Robe"},"level":"2","description":{"zh":"采用了优质的面料并带有云纹饰的长袍，衣服的边缘处也添加了华丽的纹饰。","en":"A long robe of fine fabric with cloud motifs and ornate trim."},"defenceVal":"6","hp":"780","price":"8200","slot":{"zh":"护甲","en":"Armor"}},{"id":"WP1025905","name":{"zh":"冕冠","en":"Imperial Coronet"},"level":"3","description":{"zh":"一国之主的象征。","en":"The symbol of a sovereign ruler."},"hp":"400","mp":"1200","evade":"10","price":"16000","slot":{"zh":"头盔","en":"Helmet"}}],"family":{"father":{"label":{"zh":"父亲","en":"Father"},"people":[{"id":"WJ10073","code":"0"}]},"mother":{"label":{"zh":"母亲","en":"Mother"},"people":[{"id":"WJ10179","code":"0"}]},"family":{"label":{"zh":"亲属","en":"Relatives"},"people":[{"id":"WJ1026815","code":"100"},{"id":"WJ10957","code":"100"}]}},"clans":[{"id":"GI114815","name":{"zh":"河间刘氏","en":"The Liu Clan of Hejian"},"years":["0","999"],"desc":{"zh":"普天之下莫非王土，率土之滨莫非王臣。出自姬姓，汉景帝之子河间献王刘德之后。刘德为汉景帝第三子，封河间王，谥“献”，以收集整理先秦古籍闻名。东汉时，河间王系延续，至刘开（河间孝王）时，其子刘淑封解渎亭侯，刘淑之子刘苌袭爵。刘苌早逝，其子刘宏袭解渎亭侯。永康元年，汉桓帝崩，无子，窦太后与窦武迎立刘宏为帝，是为汉灵帝。汉灵帝在位二十一年，是东汉在位时间最长的皇帝之一，但其统治时期朝政腐败、宦官专权、黄巾起义爆发，东汉帝国在他手中走向崩溃。其子刘辩（少帝）在位仅数月即被董卓所废杀；刘协（献帝）为东汉末代皇帝，被董卓、曹操先后挟持，最终禅位于曹丕，东汉灭亡。","en":"Under the vast heavens, none is not the king's land, along the shores of the realm, none is not the king's subject. Descended from the Ji surname, they trace their lineage to Liu De, Prince Xian of Hejian and son of Emperor Jing of Han. Liu De, the third son of Emperor Jing, was enfeoffed as Prince of Hejian with the posthumous title ‘Xian,’ and was celebrated for gathering and preserving pre-Qin classics. During the Eastern Han, the princely line of Hejian endured, in the time of Liu Kai (Prince Xiao of Hejian), his son Liu Shu was enfeoffed as the Marquis of Jieduting, an honor inherited by Liu Shu's son Liu Chang. Liu Chang died prematurely, whereupon his son Liu Hong inherited the marquisate. In the first year of the Yongkang era, Emperor Huan passed away without an heir, Empress Dowager Dou and Dou Wu elevated Liu Hong to the throne as Emperor Ling of Han. Reigning for twenty-one years, Emperor Ling was one of the longest-ruling emperors of the Eastern Han, yet his reign was rife with court corruption, eunuch dominance, and the outbreak of the Yellow Turban Rebellion, leading the Eastern Han Empire toward collapse in his hands. His son Liu Bian (the Young Emperor) reigned for a mere few months before being deposed and murdered by Dong Zhuo, Liu Xie (Emperor Xian) was the final emperor of the Eastern Han, coerced in succession by Dong Zhuo and Cao Cao before ultimately abdicating the throne to Cao Pi, marking the downfall of the Eastern Han."},"talent":{"military":"5","commerce":"9","politics":"8"}}],"friendGroups":[],"body":null,"honorifics":[],"selfAddress":[],"specialNames":[],"vip":{"isVIP":0,"from":"0","to":"0"},"marriage":{"aiMarriageAge":"25","startPregnantAge":"0"},"scenarios":[{"story":{"id":"S10802","name":{"zh":"黄巾起义","en":"Yellow Turban Rebellion"},"year":"184","month":"3"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1027","noRecruit":true,"reject":null,"state":"3","role":0,"stats":[47,11,51,63,72,60],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"100","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP10014","armor":"WP1018105","helmet":"WP1025905"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10215","name":{"zh":"汉末三杰","en":"Three Heroes of the Late Han"},"year":"185","month":"3"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1027","noRecruit":true,"reject":null,"state":"3","role":0,"stats":[47,11,51,63,72,60],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"100","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP10014","armor":"WP1018105","helmet":"WP1025905"},"couple":[]},{"story":{"id":"S10615","name":{"zh":"十常侍之乱","en":"Turmoil of the Ten Attendants"},"year":"188","month":"11"},"faction":null,"city":"CS1027","noRecruit":true,"reject":null,"state":"3","role":4,"stats":[47,11,51,63,72,60],"title":-1,"rank":"9","loyalty":"100","reputation":"0","equipment":{"weapon":"WP10014","armor":"WP1018105","helmet":"WP1025905"},"couple":["WJ1014815"]},{"story":{"id":"S10402